erving my ♠2 for a critical moment later is the better team strategy.\n\nReason:\nAs a peasant with 16 cards, I cannot realistically win myself. My ♠2 is my most powerful single card and should be reserved for critical moments - either to block the Landlord when they\'re about to finish, or to help my teammate gain control when they\'re close to winning. Using it now to beat a simple Ace wastes this valuable resource. Passing preserves my control card for when it truly matters.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": []}'}
